<title>USA: TABLE - BellSouth sells $500 mln in century bonds.</title>
<headline>TABLE - BellSouth sells $500 mln in century bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Bell South Capital Funding, a unit of BellSouth Corp, was priced on Tuesday via lead manager Morgan Stanley, Dean Witter, Discover &amp; Co according to a market source.</p>
<p>BORROWER BELL SOUTH CAPITAL FUNDING</p>
<p>AMT $500 MLN	 COUPON 7.12 PCT   MATURITY 7/15/2097</p>
<p>TYPE DEBENTURES    ISS PRICE 100     FIRST PAY DATE 1/15/98</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S AA1   YIELD 7.125 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P AAA	 SPREAD +60 BPS    CALLABLE MAKE WHOLE CALL</p>
<p>							    AT 15 BPS OVER</p>
<p>							    TREASURIES</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1662))</p>
</text>
